& [RequiredSurface]
  + introduce one separate safe-Rust one-shot executable named cantor-sop-inspect-stdio
  + accept no command arguments and read exactly one request byte sequence from stdin through an explicit maximum-plus-one bounded loop
  + require EOF before dispatch and refuse empty oversized malformed unknown duplicate trailing or otherwise invalid outer input without invoking semantic inspection
  + call only cantor_sop_inspect_wire respond after complete bounded input admission
  + on a valid outer request write the exact returned wire response bytes to stdout with no prefix suffix newline translation or partial alternate payload
  + treat a governed nested semantic refusal as a successfully transported wire response and preserve its exact status and fault
  + on invocation input admission outer wire or stdout completion failure emit at most one fixed bounded public fault code to stderr and return one fixed nonzero exit disposition
  + never write both a response and a host fault and never echo request bytes paths nested source or raw operating-system diagnostics
  + expose no path filesystem socket network listener service concurrency environment clock random provider model installation update remote or mutation surface
  + make process stdin stdout stderr and exit disposition the complete new authority surface and no more

& [Acceptance]
  + the same admitted stdin bytes produce the exact direct wire response bytes and successful exit disposition in fresh processes
  + malformed empty oversized extra-argument and write-failure classes remain bounded fail-closed and non-echoing
  + static inspection proves the executable imports only stdio process exit and the published wire API rather than filesystem network service provider or model surfaces
  + focused debug overflow-checked release exact workspace warnings-denied Clippy format dual-host custody formation and retained evidence gates pass before publication
  + implementation publication and immediate bookend occur only after a separately signed SJS formation and completion signature

& [NonAuthority]
  + stdio host means one process one request one response or one public host fault and does not mean a resident daemon session transport protocol or shell
  + stdin content remains caller-supplied data and never authorizes path resolution filesystem access or command execution
  + no filesystem read or write SQLite cache index socket network listener MCP LSP resident service authentication concurrency provider model inference installation update remote machine merge or product effect
  + no byte from C:\Project\Cantor is modified staged normalized copied back or deleted

& [ProcessingState]
  + preserved_unprocessed_SJS_required
